Aetherion on Debian 13
======================

The package holds Aetherion with its own Erlang runtime in /opt/aetherion, the
aetherion command, and the aetherion-worker and aetherion-agent services, which
are off until you enable them. The same package goes on the main server, on
every worker and on every machine under test with an agent.

    sudo apt install ./aetherion_<version>-1_amd64.deb


One machine
-----------

    aetherion run shop.perf --config staging.perfcfg --seed 42

Paths are relative to the directory you run it in. Ctrl+C stops the run
cleanly: the users finish their requests and Cleanup runs. The exit code is 0
when every Test passed, 1 when a Test failed and 2 when the run could not start
or finish.


A main server and workers
-------------------------

The main server runs the suite; the workers run its virtual users. Generate one
secret for all of them:

    openssl rand -hex 32

On every worker, set its name and the secret in /etc/aetherion/worker.env:

    AETHERION_NAME=euWorker1@10.0.0.11     # name@host, host = this machine's address
    AETHERION_COOKIE=<the secret>

and start the service, which also starts at boot:

    sudo systemctl enable --now aetherion-worker
    journalctl -u aetherion-worker          # "Aetherion worker euWorker1@10.0.0.11 is ready"

On the main server, name the workers in the suite's Config or in the external
configuration file:

    Config {
      workers {
        euWorker1 { host = "10.0.0.11"; }
        euWorker2 { host = "10.0.0.12"; }
        euWorker3 { host = "10.0.0.13"; }
      }
    }

and run with the same secret:

    export AETHERION_COOKIE=<the secret>
    aetherion run shop.perf --config cluster.perfcfg

--workers euWorker1@10.0.0.11,euWorker2@10.0.0.12 replaces the workers of the
Config for one run. The main server checks that it reaches every worker, and
that every worker runs the same version, before any Test starts.


Monitoring agents
-----------------

An agent measures cpu, mem, disk and net of the machine under test it runs on,
for the main server, with no node_exporter. On every such machine, set its name
and the same secret in /etc/aetherion/agent.env:

    AETHERION_NAME=sutServer1@192.168.178.91   # target@host, host = this machine's address
    AETHERION_COOKIE=<the secret>

and start the service, which also starts at boot:

    sudo systemctl enable --now aetherion-agent
    journalctl -u aetherion-agent           # "Aetherion agent sutServer1@192.168.178.91 is ready"

In the suite, the name is the target and the address its host, and
format = aetherion says that the agents measure the targets:

    Config {
      sut {
        sutServer1 { host = "192.168.178.91"; metrics = [cpu, mem, disk, net]; }
      }
      monitoring { interval = 1s; format = aetherion; }
    }

Run with the same secret, as with workers. The main server checks that it
reaches every agent, and that every agent runs the same version, before any
Test starts. A machine can run a worker and an agent; they are two nodes with
two names.


Firewall
--------

On every worker and every machine with an agent, let the main server in on:

    4369/tcp    epmd, which tells the main server the node's port
    4370/tcp    the worker, set in /etc/aetherion/worker.env
    4371/tcp    the agent, set in /etc/aetherion/agent.env

The main server needs no open port: it opens the connections. For example, with
nftables or ufw on a worker:

    sudo ufw allow from 10.0.0.10 to any port 4369,4370 proto tcp   # a worker
    sudo ufw allow from 10.0.0.10 to any port 4369,4371 proto tcp   # an agent

The secret is the only check, and nothing is encrypted. Keep the servers on a
private network, or connect them with a VPN such as WireGuard.


Upgrades
--------

Upgrade every server to the same version: the main server refuses a worker or
an agent that runs other code. Installing the package again restarts a running
worker and agent. Your /etc/aetherion/worker.env and agent.env are kept.


Removal
-------

    sudo apt remove aetherion     # keeps /etc/aetherion/worker.env and agent.env
    sudo apt purge aetherion      # removes it too
